WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.881 --> 00:00:13.100
Previously onDead City.

2
00:00:13.274 --> 00:00:13.535
- Hershel?!
- Mom!

3
00:00:15.493 --> 00:00:17.191
Name's Dillard.

4
00:00:17.365 --> 00:00:19.106
That is dastardly.

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.933
That is fresh.

6
00:00:21.108 --> 00:00:22.196
Maggie. you should
bring your people here.

7
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.415
Everything the Croat said aboutthis place is true.

8
00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:26.200
It is a fortress.

9
00:00:26.591 --> 00:00:28.680
I need this one last thing
from you.

10
00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.292
-So what kind of doctor are you?
-Emergency medicine.

11
00:00:31.466 --> 00:00:33.076
-Can I help?
-Come on.

12
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.426
Once we find the Dama.
who's left to stop us?

13
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.994
Half of Midtown is gone.

14
00:00:38.168 --> 00:00:40.214
Our work is just beginning.

15
00:03:00.441 --> 00:03:01.964
Go on and give it a shot.

16
00:04:18.736 --> 00:04:20.346
I'm just warmin' up.
though.

17
00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:22.740
Just. just gettin' it hot.
Just gettin' it spicy.

18
00:04:22.827 --> 00:04:25.700
More to come.

19
00:04:55.904 --> 00:04:57.166
Five minutes. honey.

20
00:04:58.646 --> 00:04:59.908
Yeah. I'm almost done.

21
00:05:00.996 --> 00:05:03.085
Luis said he's gonna quiz me
on this at the party.

22
00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:05.566
Thanks for usin' a drop cloth
this time

23
00:05:05.653 --> 00:05:06.654
instead of the tablecloth.

24
00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.792
Come here.

25
00:05:14.923 --> 00:05:15.924
Hi.

26
00:05:18.187 --> 00:05:19.319
I brought you
a little somethin'.

27
00:05:21.538 --> 00:05:25.237
The last bag of French roast
from Bruegel's stash.

28
00:05:26.064 --> 00:05:28.284
I'm not sure if my wife's gonna
be happier to see me or this.

29
00:05:28.937 --> 00:05:31.026
If she even recognizes you.

30
00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.202
I appreciate it.

31
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.596
I really wish
you weren't leavin'.

32
00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.641
'Cause you're gonna
miss me so much?

33
00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:41.079
-I don't like it.
-I get it.

34
00:05:42.254 --> 00:05:43.647
You're worried you're
gonna lose this place.

35
00:05:44.213 --> 00:05:45.606
You and Renata really
got something here.

36
00:05:46.171 --> 00:05:47.129
It's made you different.

37
00:05:47.782 --> 00:05:49.914
Between us gettin' captured
and almost gettin' killed.

38
00:05:50.698 --> 00:05:52.439
I used to wonder what you
were like before all this.

39
00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:55.529
Now I have some
idea.

40
00:05:55.616 --> 00:05:57.705
I'ma keep my mouth shut
about what you got here. Maggie.

41
00:05:58.662 --> 00:06:00.229
-You can trust me.
-I do...

42
00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:04.233
And I don't.

43
00:06:04.668 --> 00:06:06.670
Anybody on the road asks me
where I got this bag

44
00:06:06.757 --> 00:06:09.020
full of beans.
I'ma tell 'em the truth.

45
00:06:10.848 --> 00:06:12.023
Boston.

46
00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.680
Look. I know it's your job
to protect this place. but.

47
00:06:16.811 --> 00:06:18.029
even if I did tell anyone.

48
00:06:18.595 --> 00:06:20.771
you'd see us rollin' in
from literally a mile away.

49
00:06:20.858 --> 00:06:23.818
Luis. por favor...

50
00:06:23.905 --> 00:06:26.821
Red light. everyone. red light.
You know what to do.

51
00:06:26.908 --> 00:06:28.388
Away from the windows.
Andale.

52
00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.568
-I'll head up.
-Right behind you.

53
00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.969
Renata and Maggie are
at it again.

54
00:06:54.805 --> 00:06:56.372
Looks like a couple of
your friends from New Babaloo.

55
00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.033
Haven't seen
survivors in weeks.

56
00:07:05.512 --> 00:07:07.252
I wonder what the hell
they're doin' up here.

57
00:07:09.037 --> 00:07:10.081
You see anything?

58
00:07:10.995 --> 00:07:11.953
No.

59
00:07:13.345 --> 00:07:14.869
The Dama
needs food.

60
00:07:14.999 --> 00:07:16.218
We need food first!

61
00:07:16.348 --> 00:07:17.959
No. no. no.
she needs it first.

62
00:07:18.089 --> 00:07:19.351
I haven't eaten in
two days--

63
00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:20.483
They're tryin' to help someone.

64
00:07:20.614 --> 00:07:22.746
We feed her. She feeds us.

65
00:07:22.832 --> 00:07:26.184
The Dama feeds our minds.
our souls.

66
00:07:27.185 --> 00:07:29.187
Because we never
signed any notarized treaty

67
00:07:29.274 --> 00:07:30.362
to join their community.

68
00:07:30.711 --> 00:07:31.842
Hey. hey.

69
00:07:31.929 --> 00:07:34.932
I am asking him right now.
Stop.

70
00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:38.632
Titicaca wants to know
when the sweet jams can return.

71
00:07:38.936 --> 00:07:42.026
How many times I gotta ask you
to stop pretendin'

72
00:07:42.157 --> 00:07:44.202
like you can talk
to those toothless freaks?

73
00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:46.161
How many times do I gotta tell
you I can

74
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:47.467
decipher multiple phrases?
Desires.

75
00:07:48.206 --> 00:07:49.033
Negan. are you there?

76
00:07:49.164 --> 00:07:50.295
Okay.

77
00:07:53.429 --> 00:07:56.954
Stop light
goes on. so does the walkie.

78
00:07:57.085 --> 00:07:59.087
See. I am a good little boy.

79
00:07:59.391 --> 00:08:00.828
You got eyeballs on these guys?

80
00:08:00.958 --> 00:08:02.220
It sounds like
they're over by you.

81
00:08:03.047 --> 00:08:06.442
Limpy McGee and Trotter?
Yeah. What are they sayin'?

82
00:08:06.529 --> 00:08:09.532
They're lookin' for food
for the Dama.

83
00:08:10.838 --> 00:08:13.928
Shit. the Dama eats?
I thought she just sucked blood.

84
00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:15.451
This is what
we've been waitin' for.

85
00:08:15.582 --> 00:08:17.148
Don't tell me that you're drunk.

86
00:08:17.235 --> 00:08:19.237
No such thing.
Let's go get her.

87
00:08:19.324 --> 00:08:21.544
Okay.

88
00:08:21.936 --> 00:08:23.241
Who is the Dama?

89
00:08:23.328 --> 00:08:26.506
She is a big dick
who's about to get hers.

90
00:09:22.953 --> 00:09:24.172
I gotta tell ya. man.

91
00:09:24.302 --> 00:09:25.390
I never thought we were gonna
get rid of ya.

92
00:09:26.435 --> 00:09:27.915
Actually wantin'
to be with my family?

93
00:09:28.002 --> 00:09:31.092
-I know it's a foreign concept.
-Ouch. Well. that stings.

94
00:09:32.093 --> 00:09:33.921
See? I'll tell you why.

95
00:09:34.051 --> 00:09:36.401
'Cause the sad truth is.
Annie and Joshua?

96
00:09:36.488 --> 00:09:38.012
They are better off without me.

97
00:09:38.142 --> 00:09:41.755
I'm better off without them.

98
00:09:43.147 --> 00:09:45.802
Livin' in a bar
that smells like rotting flesh.

99
00:09:50.241 --> 00:09:51.068
Okay.

100
00:09:54.028 --> 00:09:55.856
Dama's Broadway babies!

101
00:10:14.178 --> 00:10:17.181
Who feeds us more
than merely bread?

102
00:10:17.965 --> 00:10:20.968
And fills our soul
and fills our head?

103
00:10:24.885 --> 00:10:27.975
Who kindles dreams o'er the day?

104
00:10:29.454 --> 00:10:31.805
Whose shining brilliance
guides the way?

105
00:10:34.459 --> 00:10:37.506
Who sees the future
like Nostradama?

106
00:10:38.594 --> 00:10:42.685
Who indeed. but our fair Dama?

107
00:10:47.211 --> 00:10:50.824
Well. Holy Jesus.

108
00:10:50.954 --> 00:10:54.349
I have taken
more poetic shits than that.

109
00:10:54.915 --> 00:10:56.003
We're not here to hurt you.

110
00:10:57.961 --> 00:10:58.832
That. though?

111
00:10:59.963 --> 00:11:01.704
I mean. I'm not much
of a painting guy.

112
00:11:01.835 --> 00:11:04.664
but those are some
sweet-ass boobies.

113
00:11:07.057 --> 00:11:09.581
These are the two
hilltops of kinship.

114
00:11:09.669 --> 00:11:11.583
Together. they form
the foundation of civilized--

115
00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:12.976
No. no. no. no. no. no.

116
00:11:13.107 --> 00:11:14.935
Those are boobies.

117
00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.633
Have you ever seen
an honest to God--

118
00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.591
- Are you done?
- Well. no.

119
00:11:19.722 --> 00:11:22.246
I mean. look. those are some
hot alien boobies.

120
00:11:22.986 --> 00:11:25.293
We saw you scavenging.
We brought food.

121
00:11:26.598 --> 00:11:29.166
We have more food at home
than you could eat.

122
00:11:29.906 --> 00:11:32.169
We have a doctor. too.
He can set you right.

123
00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:34.215
I'm headin' back
to New Babylon tomorrow.

124
00:11:35.172 --> 00:11:38.001
If you'd rather come home.
there's room on my boat.

125
00:11:38.349 --> 00:11:39.611
Sounds amazing.

126
00:11:40.482 --> 00:11:42.353
A bunch of strangers
who wanna help us

127
00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:44.138
and who don't want
anything from us?

128
00:11:44.268 --> 00:11:46.401
We just want you
to tell us where the Dama is.

129
00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:50.753
- That's all you have to do.
- I saved these men.

130
00:11:51.275 --> 00:11:52.233
They were injured.

131
00:11:52.363 --> 00:11:54.975
Not just their bodies.
their minds.

132
00:11:55.062 --> 00:11:57.412
They couldn't dream.
I fixed them.

133
00:11:57.499 --> 00:11:59.457
But the first thing
that you dream is

134
00:11:59.588 --> 00:12:02.722
not to let anyonestop
you from dreaming.

135
00:12:03.505 --> 00:12:07.030
You stopped Hershel.
But you didn't stop me.

136
00:12:07.161 --> 00:12:08.902
And you can't stop them.

137
00:12:09.206 --> 00:12:13.167
Yeah. I mean. however
are we gonna stop them?

138
00:12:14.081 --> 00:12:15.996
Leave now. You'll live.

139
00:12:16.083 --> 00:12:17.606
But your dreams will die.

140
00:12:18.041 --> 00:12:19.477
- Damn it.
- You are gonna get

141
00:12:19.608 --> 00:12:20.740
these boys killed!

142
00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:23.003
"Once more unto the breach.

143
00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.005
"dear friends. once more;

144
00:12:25.092 --> 00:12:27.659
or close them all up
with our English dead."

145
00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:30.401
- Go now! Please!
- "In peace..."

146
00:12:30.662 --> 00:12:31.707
Drop your weapons.

147
00:12:31.794 --> 00:12:33.578
"There's nothing
so becomes a man

148
00:12:33.709 --> 00:12:36.190
as modest stillness
and humility."

149
00:12:36.277 --> 00:12:37.582
Please just turn around.

150
00:12:37.669 --> 00:12:38.714
- All of you.
- "But. when

151
00:12:38.845 --> 00:12:40.629
the blast of war..."

152
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.631
-God damn it!
-Drop your weapons!

153
00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:44.546
"Stiffen the sinews..."

154
00:12:44.676 --> 00:12:45.765
"Summon up the blood..."

155
00:12:52.423 --> 00:12:53.903
God. that was stupid!

156
00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.128
Go.

157
00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:04.131
Go!

158
00:13:05.045 --> 00:13:05.959
Fight!

159
00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.482
Fight. you coward!

160
00:13:11.051 --> 00:13:12.443
There.

161
00:13:15.707 --> 00:13:18.275
- It's over. Dama.
- The end is

162
00:13:18.406 --> 00:13:21.017
never really the end.

163
00:13:22.236 --> 00:13:23.628
Look out!

164
00:13:28.459 --> 00:13:30.331
Son of a bitch.

165
00:13:30.461 --> 00:13:33.595
There she goes. Get up! Hurry!

166
00:13:39.296 --> 00:13:41.821
No!

167
00:14:00.622 --> 00:14:03.364
You selfish swine!

168
00:14:04.365 --> 00:14:05.757
Your son...

169
00:14:05.888 --> 00:14:09.196
was gonna shape
the future of this city.

170
00:14:10.675 --> 00:14:12.808
But you couldn't let that
happen.

171
00:14:12.939 --> 00:14:14.723
You had to lure him away.

172
00:14:16.638 --> 00:14:18.858
I will see Hershel again.
and when I do.

173
00:14:19.249 --> 00:14:21.817
he will understand the error
of his ways.

174
00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.385
Sure.

175
00:14:25.125 --> 00:14:27.736
Keep talkin'... Please.

176
00:14:27.823 --> 00:14:29.085
You don't need to kill her.

177
00:14:29.172 --> 00:14:30.043
No.

178
00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:32.523
She absolutely needs to die.

179
00:14:32.654 --> 00:14:34.177
No!

180
00:15:01.161 --> 00:15:02.379
Where's The Croat?

181
00:15:03.641 --> 00:15:05.426
He obviously built
these for you.

182
00:15:05.513 --> 00:15:06.906
Where is he?

183
00:15:07.471 --> 00:15:08.908
Dead.

184
00:15:11.954 --> 00:15:13.913
Th--and where
did you get these tanks?

185
00:15:23.183 --> 00:15:24.271
Eat.

186
00:15:25.228 --> 00:15:26.447
Not in here.

187
00:15:28.144 --> 00:15:29.406
I can't be in here.

188
00:15:31.887 --> 00:15:33.106
Why haven't you killed me yet?

189
00:15:37.849 --> 00:15:38.938
Maggie...

190
00:15:42.028 --> 00:15:43.943
I... I... I might have...

191
00:15:44.421 --> 00:15:45.683
...underestimated you.

192
00:15:46.467 --> 00:15:50.123
Maybe you are where
Hershel gets his spark.

193
00:15:51.472 --> 00:15:52.821
I wanna help. Maggie.

194
00:15:53.213 --> 00:15:55.606
I want this city to be restored.

195
00:15:56.172 --> 00:15:59.697
It's all I've ever wanted.
This hospital was a

196
00:15:59.828 --> 00:16:03.440
great start.
but you need to think bigger.

197
00:16:04.224 --> 00:16:09.794
Enough of these tanks.
you can power this whole island.

198
00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.189
We just need to talk
about it more.

199
00:16:13.755 --> 00:16:17.106
So I can paint pictures for you?

200
00:16:18.151 --> 00:16:20.327
So I can kill for you?

201
00:16:20.805 --> 00:16:25.332
I had a vision.
I have knowledge.

202
00:16:26.115 --> 00:16:28.639
Central Park used
to be farmland.

203
00:16:28.726 --> 00:16:31.686
These lofts. factories...

204
00:16:33.514 --> 00:16:38.171
There's an entire civilization
just waiting to be unleashed.

205
00:16:39.563 --> 00:16:40.869
There is.

206
00:16:44.307 --> 00:16:45.178
Maggie!

207
00:16:45.656 --> 00:16:46.657
Maggie!

208
00:16:58.713 --> 00:17:00.193
- I don't think I'm ready yet.
- You are.

209
00:17:01.977 --> 00:17:04.719
one breath. one motion.

210
00:17:05.241 --> 00:17:06.634
Hey!

211
00:17:06.763 --> 00:17:09.897
Somebody get me a goddamn
needle. I'll do it myself!

212
00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:15.164
It's just skin.
His is obviously very thin.

213
00:17:29.396 --> 00:17:32.051
So glad I get to be. like.
your practice dummy here.

214
00:17:34.966 --> 00:17:36.403
What the hell are
you even doin' here?

215
00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.274
What does it look like?

216
00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:43.323
I'm watchin' my son put a needle
through your flesh repeatedly.

217
00:17:44.193 --> 00:17:45.412
Why don't you go get your son.
like.

218
00:17:45.542 --> 00:17:47.109
a shot of hooch
to calm his nerves?

219
00:17:47.196 --> 00:17:48.632
Just 'cause you
don't like needles.

220
00:17:48.763 --> 00:17:50.547
you don't have to take
it out on him.

221
00:17:50.634 --> 00:17:52.027
Yeah.
Obviously. I have a real

222
00:17:52.114 --> 00:17:54.595
aversion to needles.
needle dick.

223
00:17:57.163 --> 00:17:58.729
Look. Sparky...

224
00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:02.124
I have saved
your life multiple times.

225
00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.300
Why are you scared of me?

226
00:18:04.387 --> 00:18:06.215
Why would anyone be
weirded out by the dude who

227
00:18:06.302 --> 00:18:07.695
spends all day
playing video games

228
00:18:07.782 --> 00:18:09.088
in his walker bar?

229
00:18:10.393 --> 00:18:11.786
I mean. how'd you even get this?

230
00:18:12.743 --> 00:18:13.875
One of those empty
bottles of yours

231
00:18:14.005 --> 00:18:15.398
try to jump out and bite ya?

232
00:18:18.445 --> 00:18:19.402
He doesn't know?

233
00:18:24.581 --> 00:18:28.411
She's downstairs.
She's locked up.

234
00:18:30.892 --> 00:18:33.982
She is never gonna hurt you.
I promise.

235
00:18:34.591 --> 00:18:36.637
There's no need to be afraid.

236
00:18:38.247 --> 00:18:40.031
I know this is wrong. but...

237
00:18:41.337 --> 00:18:45.124
I think if I was there. I would
have wanted to kill her. but...

238
00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:48.127
Everybody in
the room wanted that.

239
00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.304
But I don't know if I could've.

240
00:18:52.827 --> 00:18:57.484
Sometimes
I worry. you know.

241
00:18:57.614 --> 00:18:59.355
when it's my time
to kill a person.

242
00:19:00.139 --> 00:19:01.792
that I won't be able to do it.

243
00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.320
Is that somethin'
you can teach me?

244
00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.589
So realistically.
what are our options here?

245
00:19:15.676 --> 00:19:17.417
What?
We really just have two?

246
00:19:17.504 --> 00:19:19.723
Kill her or keep her locked
up for the rest of her life?

247
00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.464
Or we could try
to rehabilitate her.

248
00:19:21.551 --> 00:19:24.772
-You ever seen that work?
-Yeah. I have.

249
00:19:24.859 --> 00:19:26.339
You think it'll work with her?

250
00:19:26.687 --> 00:19:28.254
- I don't know.
- Okay.

251
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.128
If we keep her locked up in
jail. we are using resources.

252
00:19:33.215 --> 00:19:34.608
And I'm not just
talking about food.

253
00:19:34.738 --> 00:19:37.045
If we're sayin' that she
is so dangerous that she can't

254
00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:38.438
be outside of a cage.

255
00:19:38.525 --> 00:19:40.570
then we need someone
to guard her to make sure

256
00:19:40.657 --> 00:19:42.181
that she never gets
